When you figure out the puzzle!	等你解開謎題就知道了！
You cannot do that, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，你沒辦法這麼做。
You smell nothing unusual.	你沒有聞到什麼不尋常的味道。
Keep it to yourself.	這件事你自己知道就好。
You can't.	你辦不到。
That's strange... you don't get an answer.	真奇怪……你沒有得到任何回應。
Talking to yourself is a sure sign that the hot Daventry sun is taking its toll on you.	自言自語，肯定代表戴凡確炎熱的太陽把你曬得不輕了。
Sir Graham, please try to find another word for "%s."	格拉漢爵士，請試著為「%s」換個說法。
"%s" in "%s"	「%s」在「%s」中
Please try to rephrase that thought, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，請試著換句話說。
Please try something else, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，請試試別的辦法。
 Score: %d of %d%13s%s%1s	 得分：%d／%d%13s%s%1s
You see a useless dead goat lying lifeless on the ground.	你看見一隻毫無用處的山羊死屍，直挺挺地躺在地上。
The goat is grazing nearby.	山羊正在附近吃草。
The old goat, trotting briskly, seems happy to be with you.	這隻老山羊小跑步跟著你，看起來很開心能跟你在一起。
The goat is wandering this way and that, exploring his little pen.	山羊在牠的小圍欄裡東晃西晃，四處探索。
The goat has wandered off to the other side of his pen.	山羊已經晃到圍欄的另一邊去了。
This is the ugliest, meanest, nastiest troll you have ever seen.  And he is not about to let anybody cross his bridge.	這是你見過最醜、最兇惡、最討人厭的矮精靈。他絕不會讓任何人踏過他的橋。
There is no troll here.	這裡沒有矮精靈。
You have %d smooth, rounded pebble.	你有 %d 顆光滑圓潤的鵝卵石。
You have %d smooth, rounded pebbles.	你有 %d 顆光滑圓潤的鵝卵石。
rm%03d: %s: %s 	rm%03d: %s: %s 
It's not quite within reach, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，這東西不太搆得到。
You don't have anything that fits that description in your inventory.	你的物品欄裡沒有符合這個描述的東西。
You're too busy.	你正忙著呢。
You're too busy right now.	你現在正忙著呢。
You cannot reach the door from here.	你在這裡搆不到那扇門。
You recall a rule prohibiting goats (except seeing-eye goats) from entering the castle.	你想起有條規定禁止山羊（導盲山羊除外）進入城堡。
That's odd.  Why aren't the guards at their posts?	真奇怪，衛兵怎麼沒在崗位上？
You reconsider the wisdom of returning to King Edward without having recovered Daventry's three lost treasures.	你重新考慮了一下，還沒找回戴凡確王國失落的三件寶物就回去見愛德華國王，這樣真的明智嗎？
The portcullis is already closed.	閘門已經關上了。
Your knock echoes within the castle.  Unfortunately, no one answers.	你的敲門聲在城堡裡迴盪，可惜沒有人應門。
If you inherit the throne, you may do whatever you please with the urns.  Until then, leave them alone.	等你繼承王位之後，這些甕你要怎麼處置都行。在那之前，別去動它們。
The pots are full of dirt and roots.  There's nothing remotely helpful in or around the urns.	甕裡裝滿了泥土和根鬚，甕內外都沒有什麼派得上用場的東西。
There are no guards in sight.	附近看不到衛兵。
This deep swampy moat is patrolled by vicious serpents.	這條又深又泥濘的護城河裡，有兇猛的巨蛇巡邏。
The vines creeping up the walls of the castle are rooted in these two large urns.	攀爬城牆的藤蔓，根就扎在這兩個大甕裡。
The castle walls are carpeted with a thick tangle of vines.	城牆上爬滿了一片濃密糾結的藤蔓。
You can't see any flowers from where you stand.	你站的地方看不到任何花朵。
There are small flowers growing along the moat.	護城河邊長著一些小花。
The guards are surprised at your sudden appearance.	衛兵們對你突然出現感到十分驚訝。
Before entering the castle, you remove your ring so as not to startle the ailing King.	進城堡之前，你先取下戒指，以免驚動臥病在床的國王。
These stone-faced guards must have been trained not to converse with anybody.  They ignore you, Sir Graham.	這些面無表情的衛兵，想必受過訓練不與任何人交談。他們對你視若無睹，格拉漢爵士。
The guards are well provided-for by King Edward.  They are not interested in any of your belongings.	愛德華國王待衛兵不薄，他們對你的任何物品都沒興趣。
These are the guards of your king, King Edward.  It would be very unwise to make enemies of them, Sir Graham.	這些是你的國王——愛德華國王的衛兵。格拉漢爵士，與他們結怨可不是明智之舉。
These stone-faced guards must have been trained not to show any type of affection.  They ignore you, Sir Graham.	這些面無表情的衛兵，想必受過訓練不表露任何情感。他們對你視若無睹，格拉漢爵士。
These guards protect the King's castle.	這些衛兵負責守護國王的城堡。
Just walk up to the portcullis and open it.	只要走到閘門前把它打開就行了。
This portcullis is the only entrance to the King's castle.	這道閘門是通往國王城堡的唯一入口。
These beautiful urns adorn the front of the castle.	這些精美的甕裝飾著城堡的正面。
You never know what sort of fierce creatures lie just beneath the surface of the moat.	你永遠不知道護城河水面下潛伏著什麼兇猛的生物。
There is a hole where the rock once was.	石頭原本所在的地方，現在留下一個洞。
You're in a shady forest clearing.  A large rock rests in the middle of the clearing next to a shallow hole where the rock used to sit.	你身處一片林蔭下的空地。空地中央有塊大石頭，旁邊有個淺洞，正是這塊石頭原本擺放的地方。
You're in a shady forest clearing.  A large rock rests in the middle of the clearing.	你身處一片林蔭下的空地，空地中央有塊大石頭。
There is a shallow hole where the rock once rested in.	石頭原本擺放的地方，現在留下一個淺洞。
There is an intricately carved dagger in the hole.	洞裡有一把雕工精細的短刀。
You see a large rock resting in the middle of the clearing.	你看見空地中央擺著一塊大石頭。
There's not a lot to see except for the grass beneath your feet and a couple of large rocks.	這裡沒什麼好看的，只有腳下的草地和幾塊大石頭。
There is nothing in this hole but dirt.	這個洞裡除了泥土什麼也沒有。
You are too far away from the hole to see into it.	你離那個洞太遠，看不清裡面。
There is no hole here.	這裡沒有洞。
There's nothing interesting about the dirt.	這些泥土沒什麼特別的。
You could see it better if you picked it up.	把它撿起來，你會看得更清楚。
You do not have a dagger to look at.	你身上沒有短刀可以看。
You can't read the runes, but it appears to be an elvish dagger of great antiquity.	你看不懂上面的符文，但這似乎是一把年代久遠的小精靈短刀。
You don't have any carvings to look at.	你身上沒有任何雕刻品可以看。
You are already standing in the hole.	你已經站在洞裡了。
You can just walk right over into the hole.  It's very shallow.	你可以直接走進那個洞，洞很淺。
You don't see a hole.	你沒看到洞。
You have thrown the dagger and it is lost forever.	你已經把短刀扔出去了，永遠找不回來了。
You've already accomplished that task.	你已經完成過這件事了。
You can't pick up the dagger while you're invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法撿起短刀。
You might be able to do that if you weren't ducking!	要是你沒蹲著，也許就能做到！
You are too far away to get the dagger.	你離得太遠，拿不到短刀。
There is no dagger here.	這裡沒有短刀。
The rock is much, much harder than your foot.  You'd injure yourself.	這塊石頭比你的腳硬得多，你會弄傷自己的。
It is a large rock.  There is a shallow hole in the ground where the rock used to sit.	這是一塊大石頭，地上有個淺洞，正是這塊石頭原本擺放的地方。
You see a large, grey rock.	你看見一塊灰色的大石頭。
There's nothing useful or interesting about this rock.	這塊石頭沒什麼有用或有趣的地方。
This rock is far too heavy for you to carry.	這塊石頭太重了，你搬不動。
You are much too far away to even attempt getting the rock.	你離得太遠了，根本不用嘗試去拿那塊石頭。
The rock is far too heavy to be picked up.	這塊石頭太重了，撿不起來。
It will be very difficult to move the rock from here.	從這裡要移動這塊石頭會很困難。
After moving that rock once, just the thought of moving it again exhausts you.	你已經搬過那塊石頭一次，光是想到要再搬一次就讓你筋疲力盡。
It's pretty hard to move the rock while you're invisible.	隱形的時候，要搬動石頭相當困難。
With a small shove, you manage to push the rock a few feet... revealing a shallow hole underneath.	你輕輕一推，把石頭推開了幾步……底下露出一個淺洞。
You reach into the hole and grasp the dagger, being careful not to cut yourself.	你伸手進洞裡抓住短刀，小心翼翼不讓自己受傷。
There are many smooth pebbles next to the lake.	湖邊有許多光滑的鵝卵石。
You're standing on a pebble strewn patch of sand on the river bank.	你站在河岸上一片滿是鵝卵石的沙地上。
You see your own boot-clad feet.	你看見自己穿著靴子的雙腳。
There is a beach of pebbles on its edge.	邊上有一片鵝卵石灘。
The sandy beach along the side of the lake is strewn with small pebbles.	湖邊的沙灘上散落著許多小鵝卵石。
The only rocks of interest are some pebbles on the beach.	唯一值得注意的石頭，就是沙灘上的那些鵝卵石。
From here it looks like an ordinary beach of pebbles.	從這裡看，這只是一片普通的鵝卵石灘。
The only rocks worth getting are some pebbles on the beach.	唯一值得撿的石頭，就是沙灘上的那些鵝卵石。
You are not close enough to the pebbles to get them.	你離鵝卵石不夠近，撿不到。
Your pockets cannot hold any more pebbles.	你的口袋裝不下更多鵝卵石了。
You can't pick up any of the pebbles while you are invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法撿起任何鵝卵石。
You grab a handful of pebbles.	你抓了一把鵝卵石。
You grab a pebble.	你撿起一顆鵝卵石。
You grab some pebbles.	你撿起幾顆鵝卵石。
As you slip into the water, the magic ring slips from your finger.	你滑入水中時，魔戒從你的手指上滑落了。
That's one giant leap for the fish!	對這條魚來說，這可是一大步啊！
Looks like all the fish are currently underwater.	看來所有的魚現在都在水面下。
The fish would make your clothes smell and wouldn't be any help on your quest.	那條魚只會讓你的衣服發臭，對你的冒險毫無幫助。
This is a serene mountain lake.	這是一座寧靜的山中湖泊。
In the woods to the north, you can just see what looks like an old stone well.	在北邊的樹林裡，你隱約看見一口像是古老石井的東西。
The sunlight glistens on the rippling water.	陽光在粼粼水波上閃耀。
Do you see any fish here at the moment?	你現在有看到任何魚嗎？
Perhaps you'll find a use for a fish in a different King's Quest, but not in this one.	也許在另一款《國王密令》裡，魚會派上用場，但這一款不會。
You already have the pouch.	你已經拿到皮袋了。
You found it already.	你已經找到了。
Haven't you found it yet?	你還沒找到嗎？
Inside the rotting stump you notice a small leather pouch.	你在腐朽的樹樁裡發現一個小皮袋。
Inside the decaying tree stump, you see nothing interesting.	在這個腐朽的樹樁裡，你沒看到什麼特別的東西。
Why don't you move closer to try that?	你何不靠近一點再試試看？
You peer into the darkness inside the log, but there's nothing at all inside.	你窺探樹幹內部的黑暗，但裡面什麼也沒有。
You're not close enough to see into the log.	你離得不夠近，看不進樹幹裡面。
From here you can see the stump is very old and rotting away.	從這裡你看得出這個樹樁又老又朽。
You can only vaguely see the stump from this distance.	隔著這段距離，你只能隱約看見那個樹樁。
Next to you is an old fallen tree trunk.  It's crumbling and rotted, and holds no interest for you... unless you have a fascination with termites!	你身旁有一根倒下的老樹幹，已經腐朽崩解，沒什麼好看的……除非你對白蟻特別著迷！
You can't see much of the log from over here.	從這裡看不清楚那根樹幹。
You're in a quiet part of the forest.  There's an old rotted stump here.	你身處森林一處僻靜的地方，這裡有個腐朽的老樹樁。
You can't see the termites unless you split open the log.  But that would be a waste of time.	除非劈開樹幹，否則你看不到白蟻，但那只是浪費時間。
You're not that hungry.  You hope that you NEVER become that hungry!	你沒那麼餓，你希望自己永遠都不會餓成那樣！
They're obviously more afraid of you than you are of them.  Leave them alone.	顯然牠們比你還怕，別去招惹牠們。
There is no reason to take this old log with you.	沒有理由把這根老樹幹帶在身上。
You are already carrying them in your leather pouch.	你已經把它們裝在皮袋裡帶著了。
You already have the leather pouch.	你已經有這個皮袋了。
There's no pouch here.	這裡沒有皮袋。
